```
#reason: The question asks for the weekly average mean temperature for parts of the Thessaly Region with lakes during week 12 of 2020. This requires filtering meteo_tmean data by: (1) geographic bounds from GEO_CONTEXT (Thessaly Region points), (2) landcover type being lakes (which corresponds to level3_label = 'Inland waters' from the provided value), and (3) time being week 12 of 2020. Since landcover_upscaled contains latitude/longitude and ranks (which must be expanded to link to landcover_type.level3_label), we must UNNEST the ranks and join with landcover_type to filter for 'Inland waters'. Then, we join with meteo_tmean on matching latitude and longitude, filter for week 12 of 2020, and compute the average of tmean.
#columns: meteo_tmean.tmean, landcover_type.level3_label, landcover_upscaled.latitude, landcover_upscaled.longitude, meteo_tmean.time
#values: 'lakes' refer to landcover_type.level3_label: 'Inland waters', week 12 of 2020 refer to EXTRACT(WEEK FROM meteo_tmean.time) = 12 AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM meteo_tmean.time) = 2020, Thessaly Region refer to meteo_tmean.latitude BETWEEN 39.0 AND 40.0 AND meteo_tmean.longitude BETWEEN 21.2 AND 24.4
#SELECT: AVG(meteo_tmean.tmean)
#SQL: SELECT AVG(m.tmean) 
FROM meteo_tmean m
JOIN landcover_upscaled l ON m.latitude = l.latitude AND m.longitude = l.longitude
JOIN (
    SELECT UNNEST(ranks) AS rank, latitude, longitude 
    FROM landcover_upscaled
) AS unnested_l ON l.latitude = unnested_l.latitude AND l.longitude = unnested_l.longitude
JOIN landcover_type lt ON unnested_l.rank = lt.level3_label
WHERE lt.level3_label = 'Inland waters'
  AND EXTRACT(WEEK FROM m.time) = 12 
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM m.time) = 2020
  AND m.latitude BETWEEN 39.0 AND 40.0
  AND m.longitude BETWEEN 21.2 AND 24.4;
```

